    "notes": "Schedule #1 (pages 10-13 in the ToC) covers Theatrical Motion Pictures and certain TV categories at undiscounted rates; the 8/2/26-7/31/27 printing appears only on PDF page 13. Schedule #14 (pages 50-53 in the ToC) is the corresponding Distant Location schedule also covering Theatrical Motion Pictures at undiscounted rates; its 8/2/26-7/31/27 printing appears only on PDF page 53. Schedule #9 covers Preparation Pay (not studio/distant minimums) for theatrical pictures and was excluded as it is a distinct pay category, not the studio or distant location minimum wage schedule requested. Schedules #2-8, 10-13, and 15-16 all involve 3% reductions, one-year lag, two-year lag, or long-form sideletter terms, which excludes them per the prompt's criteria. Schedules #17-18 cover Coordinators/Writers' Room Assistants, unrelated to Script Supervisors' studio/distant schedules."
